# The kernel's burn-down list against termlens: one `fixture/aspect` per line (tests/oracle.rs).
# Lower is better, and it only shrinks — a key that stops disagreeing must be removed.
# Seeded 2026-09-19 at 21; 7 after slice 3a surfaced what vt100 0.15 already tracks (grid rows —
# the wrap/text defect — cursor position and visibility, italic/underline/reverse, title,
# alternate screen, input modes). What remains is what vt100 0.15 does not track.

# Cursor shape (DECSCUSR).
cursor_shape_bar/cursor_shape
cursor_shape_block/cursor_shape

# The query responder (DA1 here): a capability probe waits out its timeout against the kernel.
query_device_attributes/text

# SGR attributes vt100 0.15 drops.
sgr_attrs/cell(0,1).dim
sgr_attrs/cell(0,4).blink
sgr_attrs/cell(0,6).conceal
sgr_attrs/cell(0,7).strikethrough
